url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mrdoob/three.js/issues/comments/148863233","html_url":"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/issues/7365#issuecomment-148863233","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mrdoob/three.js/issues/7365","id":148863233,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0ODg2MzIzMw==","user":{"login":"jarethgk","id":12203722,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMjAzNzIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12203722?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarethgk","html_url":"https://github.com/jarethgk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarethgk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarethgk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarethgk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarethgk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarethgk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarethgk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarethgk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarethgk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarethgk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-10-16T23:15:36Z","updated_at":"2015-10-16T23:20:58Z","body":"The 3d object being loaded is made in Maya, and is exported as an FBX which is then loaded into Clara.IO, and then exported out as the \"ThreeJS (.json)\".\n\nI think it is getting into the \"$scope.bodyLoader_onComplete()\" and during the processing of putting it in the scene it is stumbling on the three.js code I mentioned above.\n\n``` javascript\n        $scope.skeletal_Loader = new THREE.ObjectLoader();\n        $scope.skeletal_Loader.load(\"models/skeleton/male-skeleton-ao.json\",\n        //$scope.skeletal_Loader.load(\"models/altTextures/skeletal/skeleton-landmarks.json\",\n            function(obj){ $scope.bodyLoader_onComplete(obj, $rootScope.SYSTEM_NAME.SKELETAL.WORD); },\n            function(xhr){ $scope.bodyLoader_onProgress(xhr, $rootScope.SYSTEM_NAME.SKELETAL.WORD); },\n            function(xhr){ $scope.bodyLoader_onError   (xhr, $rootScope.SYSTEM_NAME.SKELETAL.WORD); }\n        );\n```\n\n``` javascript\n    $scope.bodyLoader_onComplete = function(obj, objLoadedName) { // onComplete\n        //console.log(\"Starting onComplete function for: \" + objLoadedName);\n        //console.log(obj);\n        $scope.bodySystem[objLoadedName] = obj;\n\n        if (objLoadedName == $rootScope.SYSTEM_NAME.SKELETAL.WORD ||\n            objLoadedName == $rootScope.SYSTEM_NAME.NERVOUS.WORD ||\n            objLoadedName == $rootScope.SYSTEM_NAME.ENDOCRINE.WORD\n        ) $scope.bodySystem[objLoadedName].rotation.y = Math.PI;\n\n        $scope.bodySystem[objLoadedName].traverse(function(child) {\n            child.name = child.name.toLowerCase();\n            child.visible = true;\n            child.frustumCulled = false;\n            if (typeof child.material != \"undefined\") if (child.material != null) {\n                child.material.transparent = false;\n                child.material.opacity = 1;\n                if (objLoadedName == $rootScope.REGION_2_NAME.SKIN_MALE.WORD) {\n                    child.material.transparent = true;\n                    child.material.opacity = $scope.model_transparent;\n                }\n                child.material.shininess = 15;\n                //child.material.bumpScale = 0.12; // Uncomment and alter if default level of bumpiness is inappropriate. Save in case it needs to be changed.\n                child.material_original = child.material; // Always clone the material last.\n            }\n        });\n\n        //console.log(\"About to add to scene: \" + objLoadedName);\n        $scope.scene.add($scope.bodySystem[objLoadedName]);\n        //console.log($scope.bodySystem[objLoadedName]);\n        console.log(\"Done loading. Adding to scene. (\" + objLoadedName + \") \");\n\n        if (objLoadedName == $rootScope.SYSTEM_NAME.SKELETAL.WORD) $scope.spriteLoader();\n        if (typeof $scope.bodySystem[$rootScope.SYSTEM_NAME.SKELETAL.WORD] != \"undefined\") $scope.addedToScene = true;\n\n        $rootScope.changeSystemState($rootScope.systemState); // Must be after \"addedToScene = true\" or it won't properly fire off.\n        $scope.$apply();\n    };\n```\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mrdoob/three.js/issues/comments/148863233/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"jarethgk","id":12203722,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMjAzNzIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12203722?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarethgk","html_url":"https://github.com/jarethgk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarethgk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarethgk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarethgk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarethgk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarethgk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarethgk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarethgk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarethgk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarethgk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mrdoob/three.js/issues/comments/148894968","html_url":"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/issues/7365#issuecomment-148894968","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mrdoob/three.js/issues/7365","id":148894968,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0ODg5NDk2OA==","user":{"login":"mkkellogg","id":6249005,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNDkwMDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6249005?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkkellogg","html_url":"https://github.com/mkkellogg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkkellogg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkkellogg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkkellogg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkkellogg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkkellogg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkkellogg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkkellogg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkkellogg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkkellogg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-10-17T08:16:17Z","updated_at":"2015-10-17T08:16:17Z","body":"@jarethgk\n\nIt sounds like your instance of `THREE.WebGLRenderer` does not have shadows enabled, but you have them enabled on a point light in your scene. When shadowing is disabled in `THREE.WebGLRenderer`, `shadow.matrix` will be null. Admittedly, the code in `refreshUniformsShadow()` should do a proper check either for enabled shadows or at the very least should check if `shadow.matrix` is null. \n\nI am not familiar with how Clara.io works - how easy would it be to verify that your renderer has shadowing enabled?\n","author_associa